  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A firework rocket is launched vertically upwards and it explodes when it reaches a height of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> m. What is true about the kinetic energy and the momentum of the system when compared right before and right after the explosion?</p>\n\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Kinetic energy</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Momentum</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"A\">\n<td><strong>A.</strong></td>\n<td>Conserved</td>\n<td>Conserved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"B\">\n<td><strong>B.</strong></td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"C\">\n<td><strong>C.</strong></td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n<td>Conserved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"D\">\n<td><strong>D.</strong></td>\n<td>Conserved</td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
  },
